---
title: "Spinner"
description: "Indeterminate loading indicator for waits of unknown length."
tags: [feedback, accessibility, css]
usage: |
  Add the `spinner` class and `role="status"` to an element, with a
  `spinner-label` child holding the text to announce. Set `data-size` to `small`
  or `large`. Use Progress instead when you know how far along the work is.
accessibility: |
  - The label is visually hidden but announced through the status role.
  - When text is shown next to the spinner, hide that copy with
    `aria-hidden="true"` so it is not read twice.
  - The rotation slows down when the person prefers reduced motion.
customProperties:
  "--spinner-size": "Diameter; `data-size` changes it."
  "--spinner-width": "Width of the ring."
  "--spinner-color": "Color of the moving part."
  "--spinner-track": "Color of the rest of the ring."
  "--spinner-speed": "Time for one rotation."
---

<link rel="stylesheet" href="./styles.css" media="screen">

<span class="spinner" role="status">
  <span class="spinner-label">Loading</span>
</span>
<span class="spinner" role="status" data-size="small">
  <span class="spinner-label">Loading</span>
</span>
<span class="spinner" role="status" data-size="large">
  <span class="spinner-label">Loading</span>
</span>

<p>
  <span class="spinner" role="status" data-size="small">
    <span class="spinner-label">Saving</span>
  </span>
  <span aria-hidden="true">Saving&hellip;</span>
</p>
